# Config page renderers (Q126)

## Invariant — one ConfigPage everywhere

- **Only** `WTTConfigRender.renderPage(node, ctx)` paints the node configuration page.
- Changing a **box** renderer updates the page **everywhere**.
- Alias: `WTTSettingsRender` === `WTTConfigRender`.

## Vertical boxes (top → bottom)

| Box id | Contents |
|--------|----------|
| `actions` | Toolbar, banners |
| `meta` | Chips only (ID, Parent, Slug, …) |
| `identitySettings` | Name, Default, non-bool type extras (Footer-Op, set separator, …) |
| `bools` | Flags only, 5/row (RO, template, required) |
| `childNodes` | Kindknoten activation (e.g. allowed prefixes); **omit** if unused |
| `display` | Presentation + Preferred |
| `attributes` | Attributes list/input (Relations are separate) |
| `preview` | `WTTObjectRender` |
| `relations` | **Last** |

## Walk / Verdeckung (target policy)

- Settings subset may walk subnode settings; **stop per attribute when covered** (own or intermediate node).
- Always **peek +1** under cover; missing deeper level → mark **invalid**.
- Prefer **walk on open**, not denormalized sync lists.

## Do / don’t

- **Do** put new chrome in the matching box.
- **Don’t** mix Kindknoten into `bools` or Meta into identity.
- **Don’t** paint config outside `renderPage`.

Related: [node-renderers.mdc](node-renderers.mdc), [admin-ux-controls.mdc](admin-ux-controls.mdc).
